Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• lap_positions.lap_type : filter pure “Race” laps only, ignore other lap classifications (e.g. “Starting Position – Grid Drop”).  
• lap_positions.race_id / driver_id / lap / position : core data set to follow every driver’s on‑track position each lap – needed to detect when a driver’s position changes relative to the previous lap (gains = overtakes made, losses = overtaken).  
• pit_stops.race_id / driver_id / lap : laps when a driver enters the pit lane; position changes that occur on these laps (and the next lap when the driver rejoins) must be excluded.  
• retirements.race_id / driver_id / lap : laps on which a driver retires; position changes caused by a retirement (usually the lap on which the retirement happens) have to be excluded.  
• lap_positions.lap = 1 : represents the first racing lap; all start‑lap position changes must be ignored.  
• drivers_ext.driver_id / full_name  (or drivers.full_name) : allows us to return the full driver names once the net‑overtake calculation is complete.  

Typical filtering conditions  
• lap_positions.lap_type = 'Race'  
• lap_positions.lap > 1                                  -- skip opening‑lap movements  
• lap_positions.lap NOT IN ( … pit_stops … )             -- exclude laps with pit entries/exits  
• lap_positions.lap NOT IN ( … retirements … )           -- exclude laps with retirements  
• Δposition < 0  ➔ “overtakes made”,  Δposition > 0 ➔ “overtaken”  

Ten exploratory SQL queries (from simple inspection to a complete answer‑level draft).  
Each query is independent, uses SELECT only, includes a short description, and limits output to 20 rows.

```sql
-- 1️⃣ Description: Peek at raw lap‑by‑lap positions for a couple of drivers in one race
SELECT *
FROM lap_positions
WHERE race_id = 1
  AND driver_id IN (1,2)
ORDER BY driver_id, lap
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2️⃣ Description: Which different lap_type values exist in lap_positions?
SELECT DISTINCT lap_type
FROM lap_positions
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3️⃣ Description: View all pit‑stop laps for the same race
SELECT race_id, driver_id, lap
FROM pit_stops
WHERE race_id = 1
ORDER BY driver_id, lap
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4️⃣ Description: Laps in which retirements occurred (to be filtered out later)
SELECT race_id, driver_id, lap, status_id
FROM retirements
ORDER BY race_id, lap
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5️⃣ Description: Build a driver‑lap table that already excludes non‑race laps and lap‑1
SELECT race_id, driver_id, lap, position
FROM lap_positions
WHERE lap_type = 'Race'
  AND lap > 1
ORDER BY race_id, driver_id, lap
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6️⃣ Description: Add previous‑lap position with a self‑join (basis for Δposition)
SELECT curr.race_id, curr.driver_id, curr.lap,
       prev.position AS prev_pos,
       curr.position AS curr_pos,
       (prev.position - curr.position) AS delta_position
FROM lap_positions AS curr
JOIN lap_positions AS prev
  ON prev.race_id  = curr.race_id
 AND prev.driver_id = curr.driver_id
 AND prev.lap       = curr.lap - 1
WHERE curr.lap_type = 'Race'
  AND curr.lap      > 1
ORDER BY curr.driver_id, curr.lap
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7️⃣ Description: Exclude laps that coincide with the driver’s own pit entry
WITH p AS (
  SELECT race_id, driver_id, lap
  FROM pit_stops
)
SELECT c.*
FROM (
    SELECT curr.race_id, curr.driver_id, curr.lap,
           prev.position AS prev_pos,
           curr.position AS curr_pos,
           (prev.position - curr.position) AS delta_position
    FROM lap_positions AS curr
    JOIN lap_positions AS prev
      ON prev.race_id  = curr.race_id
     AND prev.driver_id = curr.driver_id
     AND prev.lap       = curr.lap - 1
    WHERE curr.lap_type = 'Race'
      AND curr.lap      > 1
) AS c
LEFT JOIN p
  ON p.race_id  = c.race_id
 AND p.driver_id = c.driver_id
 AND p.lap       = c.lap
WHERE p.lap IS NULL                -- keep only laps without a pit entry
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8️⃣ Description: Also remove laps affected by any retirements in the field
WITH clean_moves AS (
    SELECT curr.race_id, curr.driver_id, curr.lap,
           prev.position AS prev_pos,
           curr.position AS curr_pos,
           (prev.position - curr.position) AS delta_position
    FROM lap_positions AS curr
    JOIN lap_positions AS prev
      ON prev.race_id  = curr.race_id
     AND prev.driver_id = curr.driver_id
     AND prev.lap       = curr.lap - 1
    WHERE curr.lap_type = 'Race'
      AND curr.lap      > 1
      AND (curr.race_id, curr.driver_id, curr.lap) NOT IN (
            SELECT race_id, driver_id, lap
            FROM pit_stops
          )
)
SELECT cm.*
FROM clean_moves cm
LEFT JOIN retirements r
  ON r.race_id = cm.race_id
 AND r.lap     = cm.lap
WHERE r.lap IS NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9️⃣ Description: Count overtakes made (+) vs lost (–) for each driver across all races
WITH delta AS (
    SELECT curr.race_id, curr.driver_id,
           (prev.position - curr.position) AS delta_pos
    FROM lap_positions AS curr
    JOIN lap_positions AS prev
      ON prev.race_id  = curr.race_id
     AND prev.driver_id = curr.driver_id
     AND prev.lap       = curr.lap - 1
    WHERE curr.lap_type = 'Race'
      AND curr.lap      > 1
      AND (curr.race_id, curr.driver_id, curr.lap) NOT IN (
            SELECT race_id, driver_id, lap FROM pit_stops
          )
      AND (curr.race_id, curr.driver_id, curr.lap) NOT IN (
            SELECT race_id, driver_id, lap FROM retirements
          )
)
SELECT driver_id,
       SUM(CASE WHEN delta_pos > 0 THEN 0         -- position worsened (overtaken)
                WHEN delta_pos < 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS overtakes_made,
       SUM(CASE WHEN delta_pos > 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)             AS times_overtaken
FROM delta
GROUP BY driver_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 🔟 Description: Final step – list full names of drivers who were overtaken more often
WITH delta AS (
    SELECT curr.race_id, curr.driver_id,
           (prev.position - curr.position) AS delta_pos
    FROM lap_positions AS curr
    JOIN lap_positions AS prev
      ON prev.race_id  = curr.race_id
     AND prev.driver_id = curr.driver_id
     AND prev.lap       = curr.lap - 1
    WHERE curr.lap_type = 'Race'
      AND curr.lap      > 1
      AND (curr.race_id, curr.driver_id, curr.lap) NOT IN (
            SELECT race_id, driver_id, lap FROM pit_stops
          )
      AND (curr.race_id, curr.driver_id, curr.lap) NOT IN (
            SELECT race_id, driver_id, lap FROM retirements
          )
)
, stats AS (
    SELECT driver_id,
           SUM(CASE WHEN delta_pos < 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS overtakes_made,
           SUM(CASE WHEN delta_pos > 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS times_overtaken
    FROM delta
    GROUP BY driver_id
)
SELECT d.full_name
FROM stats s
JOIN drivers_ext d  ON d.driver_id = s.driver_id
WHERE s.times_overtaken > s.overtakes_made
LIMIT 20;
```
